From 19ca047b8e185fac64f6af0626f488b0027637e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dcasati <dcasati@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:32:39 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] tests: hook LinuxKPI wlan test modules into Kyua

Add tests/sys/compat/linuxkpi so the LinuxKPI 802.11 harnesses from
sys/tests/linuxkpi_wlan run under kyua(1) and install to
/usr/tests/sys/compat/linuxkpi.

wlan_kmod_test (atf-sh, root, exclusive) wraps the kernel test modules.
They run their checks from MOD_LOAD, so a failing module makes kldload(8)
fail with ENOEXEC and logs "MOD_LOAD (<name>, ...) error"; a passing one
prints a fixed "passed" line.  Each case requires both a successful
kldload and a new pass line in the message buffer, then unloads the
module; a cleanup routine unloads it if the body did not.  Cases skip if
the module is already loaded, if it cannot be found, or if LinuxKPI,
linuxkpi_wlan or wlan are not already present (checked through their
sysctl nodes, as they may be compiled into the kernel); the tests never
load or unload those dependencies themselves.
  - compat: lkpi_wlan_test (queues, RCU, lists, guards, tasklets, IEs,
    skbs, rhashtable).  No hardware.
  - regulatory: lkpi_regulatory_test (channel/rule translation, strict
    TX gating).  No hardware.
  - mhi: lkpi_mhi_test (MHI/QMI/CE/HTC/WMI models plus the MHI DMA
    context layout).  It allocates DMA for an unbound WCN7850 at a fixed
    address, so it requires the linuxkpi_mhi_pci=yes configuration
    variable, an ATH12KHOST or ATH12KLAB kernel and an unattached
    17cb:1107 function there; otherwise it skips without loading.

dp_cc_test and station_port_test are the userland builds of the DP
cookie layout and controlled-port checks; they need neither root nor
hardware.

The test modules are not part of buildkernel (neither is if_ath12k).
Install them from sys/modules/tests/linuxkpi_{wlan,regulatory,mhi}, or
point the tests at a build directory:

  kyua -v test_suites.FreeBSD.linuxkpi_kmod_dir=/path/to/ko \
      test -k /usr/tests/sys/compat/linuxkpi/Kyuafile

lkpi_mhi_boot attaches to the PCI device and stays out.  The Python
drivers compile pieces of the source tree with cc(1) at run time,
qmi_codec_test needs kernel build options, and station_acceptance.sh
drives a real AP from the lab guest; none of them can run from
/usr/tests, so they remain source-tree tools.

ktest(9) is not used yet: its only runner in stable/15 is
atf_python/pytest over netlink, which would make python3 and pytest
mandatory and requires restructuring every module into ktest cases.
That remains the path for upstreaming.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
